    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="1043" n="929" xml:id="pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">325.1121 Bethune, Larry K./3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-19T16:00:00-04:00">March 19, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:53 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Referring to the Department’s No. 10, March 19, 1 p.m. Bethune was released
                    today on bond but nevertheless I have presented our views on incommunicado in a
                    note to the Foreign Office.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d824-f1"/></p>
                <p>Charges against him are for fraud. Criminal proceedings were instituted by former
                    Chilean agent of General Motors to help them in pending civil suits. Strong
                    indications that proceedings are in the nature of malicious prosecution and I
                    therefore have submitted to the Government informally evidence which indicates
                    this misuse of criminal proceedings in the courts.…</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
